<h2>What stays the same everywhere we work</h2>
<p>Wherever your property is located, the process is the same: a Free Claim Review, a written contract with fees disclosed before any work begins, a thorough inspection, careful documentation, and ongoing communication with your insurer. Texas law caps public adjuster compensation at 10% of the insurance settlement, and you may rescind the contract within 72 hours of signing.</p>
<p>The region also shares a few insurance realities. It is outside the Texas Windstorm Insurance Association (TWIA) area, so wind and hail coverage typically comes from your regular insurer. Many policies carry separate wind/hail deductibles, so check your declarations page. Standard policies generally exclude flood, which matters in Flash Flood Alley. And each suburban city, as well as unincorporated Bexar County, has its own permit office, so code and permit requirements can differ from one side of a city limit to the other.</p>
<p>We handle <a href="/services/hail-damage-claims/">hail</a>, <a href="/services/wind-damage-claims/">wind</a>, <a href="/services/roof-damage-insurance-claims/">roof</a>, <a href="/services/flood-damage-claims/">flood</a>, <a href="/services/freeze-damage-claims/">freeze</a>, <a href="/services/fire-damage-claims/">fire</a>, and <a href="/services/water-damage-claims/">water damage</a> claims, for both <a href="/services/residential-property-claims/">residential</a> and <a href="/services/commercial-property-claims/">commercial</a> properties. Not sure if we cover your area? Request a <a href="/free-claim-review/">Free Claim Review</a> or call [[phone]].</p>
